{"version":1,"reference":{"kind":"artifact_content","namespace":"#3062","artifact_type":"_dh-work-item-head-v1","name":"head"},"owner_reference":"#3062","content":"{\"version\":1,\"issue_reference\":\"#3062\",\"parent_revision\":\"7c92d91cb3f029a1f8290166cb26262468c1ab96\",\"root_revision\":\"102440addc9a419a63baa60a413099cc9290783896aaa5a06f9d270b240745d5\",\"body\":\"<!-- backlog-metadata:\\npriority: \\ntype: Feature\\nstatus: open\\nadded: \\n-->\\n\\n## Description\\n\\nPagination has no content identity. Page structures carry a page number and total, but nothing identifying which document they page. Across stateless invocations a caller cannot request \\\"the next page of what you just returned\\\" \u2014 every page request re-collects from the provider and re-parses.\\n\\nThis is also a correctness gap: if content changes between page requests, pages from two different versions can be returned as though they were one document.\\n\\n## RT-ICA\\n\\n<div><sub>2026-08-20T09:11:49.444303Z</sub>\\n\\nRT-ICA Snapshot: feat: address paginated content by content identity\\nDate: 2026-08-20\\nGoal: Implement the content-identity-addressed control set (R8 of the markdown-consumption contract) so paginated/navigable responses are addressable and re-servable without re-collecting from source or redoing Generation, per ADR-3082-1's finalized design.\\nConditions:\\n1. content_id derivation rule (command + Generation output binding, not raw source or generated content alone) | Status: AVAILABLE\\n2. Storage schema (content_id PK, source, command, content, stale marker, timestamps) | Status: AVAILABLE\\n3. Storage location convention (state_root()/control-set.db, WAL mode) | Status: AVAILABLE\\n4. Eviction/cleanup policy parameters (40MB soft target, LRU-by-size, periodic rate-limited hourly-to-daily sweep) | Status: AVAILABLE\\n5. Which existing write paths across the codebase must trigger invalidation (marking a matching content_id stale) | Status: DERIVABLE\\n6. Where the Navigation stage currently lives in code (progressive_markdown package) and what wiring is needed to route through the new control set | Status: DERIVABLE\\n7. FileCache/GitHubContentCache boundary \u2014 confirmed unrelated to the control set, must not be conflated | Status: AVAILABLE\\n8. task_status_hook.py's exact current location and shape (flagged by cross-session review as a future required invalidation-trigger caller) | Status: MISSING\\n9. Concurrent-writer hardening scope confirmed deferred to #3081, not blocking this item's baseline single-writer path | Status: AVAILABLE\\n10. Existing test patterns for backend/provider code in this plugin to follow | Status: DERIVABLE\\nAVAILABLE count: 6\\nDERIVABLE count: 3\\nMISSING count: 1\\n</div>\\n\\n## Acceptance Criteria\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- [ ] A paginated response returns a stable identifier derived from the content it paginates\\n- [ ] A later page is requested with that identifier plus a page selector or address\\n- [ ] Serving a later page does not re-collect from the provider and does not re-parse\\n- [ ] A request whose identifier no longer matches current content is reported stale, not served\\n</div>\\n\\n## Context\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- **Priority**: P1\\n- Intended behaviour is defined in `plugins/development-harness/docs/agent-markdown-consumption-contract.md`. Component ownership is defined in `plugins/development-harness/docs/component-architecture.md`. Parent: #3054.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Open Decisions\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nCache scope (session-lived or persisted) and whether the identifier derives from raw markdown or the parsed tree are recorded as open questions in the contract.\\n</div>\\n\",\"digest\":\"8004d76a1b05578baaef7cdff8aa9410a90d0900b26a3d2d01191cc611e24144\",\"comment_id\":\"IC_kwDOQGimCs8AAAABPx08ag\"}"}